WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:08.813
Open the project, and create one more model in models: monthly summary dot sql.

00:00:13.857 --> 00:00:17.994
First, a block called totals: the trips per month, from ref trips per month.

00:00:20.624 --> 00:00:25.845
Then a block called card: the trips paid by credit card each month, straight from ref trips.

00:00:27.257 --> 00:00:30.522
Join them by month, and work out the percent paid by card.

00:00:30.802 --> 00:00:31.401
Save.

00:00:34.665 --> 00:00:40.252
Describe it too: at the end of schema dot yml, paste the entry for monthly summary, and save.

00:00:41.202 --> 00:00:43.327
All those refs form a graph: the DAG.

00:00:43.607 --> 00:00:46.058
Directed, because every arrow points one way.

00:00:46.338 --> 00:00:49.043
Acyclic, because no model can depend on itself.

00:00:49.993 --> 00:00:56.975
dbt uses it for the build order, to run independent models in parallel, and to show you what a change affects.

00:00:57.925 --> 00:01:02.954
Back in monthly summary, open the Model menu, and choose Run plus model, upstream.

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:05.954
That runs this model, and everything it depends on.

00:01:06.904 --> 00:01:11.102
Three models, in DAG order: trips, trips per month, then monthly summary.

00:01:12.052 --> 00:01:12.990
Now the docs.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:22.044
Open the Project menu, and choose Generate Docs. dbt reads the project and the database, and writes a small website into target.

00:01:22.994 --> 00:01:24.561
Then Project, Serve Docs.

00:01:24.841 --> 00:01:28.013
Studio starts a local web server, on port eighty eighty.

00:01:29.476 --> 00:01:34.212
In the browser, open localhost, port eighty eighty, and pick monthly summary.

00:01:34.492 --> 00:01:39.754
Here is the description from schema dot yml, every column, and what the model depends on.

00:01:40.704 --> 00:01:47.940
The button at the bottom right opens the lineage graph: the whole DAG, from the raw source and the seed, to monthly summary.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:53.734
Back in Studio, the Git tab shows the new model, and the change to schema dot yml.

00:01:54.684 --> 00:01:58.384
Stage all, type a message, add the monthly summary, and commit.

00:02:03.284 --> 00:02:05.319
Sync Changes, and it's on GitHub.

00:02:08.384 --> 00:02:13.103
To recap: refs form the DAG, and dbt uses it for order and impact.

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:16.720
Run plus model builds a model with everything upstream.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.990
And two clicks give you a docs site, with descriptions and the lineage graph.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:24.084
Next, views or tables: materializations.
